spans.s:
सम्-√ पत् P. -पतति, to fly or rush together (in a friendly or hostile manner), encounter, meet any one (acc.), meet with (instr.), RV. &c. &c.;
to fly along, fly to, hasten towards, arrive at, reach (acc. or loc.), AitBr.; MBh. &c.;
to fly or fall down, alight on (loc.), MBh.;
to go or roam about, R.; VarBṛS.;
to come to pass, take place, happen, occur, MBh.; Hariv. :
Caus. -पातयति, to cause to fly or fall, throw or hurl down, R.; BhP.

सम्-√ पद् Ā. -पद्यते (in some forms also P.; ind.p. -पादम्, q.v.),
to fall or happen well, turn out well, succeed, prosper, accrue to (dat. or gen.), AV. &c. &c.;
to become full or complete (as a number), amount to, Br.; ChUp.; Hariv.;
to fall together, meet or unite with, obtain, get into, partake of (instr. or acc.), Br.; Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to enter into, be absorbed in (acc. or loc.), ChUp.; BhP.;
to be produced, be brought forth, be born, arise, MBh.; R.;
to become, prove, turn into (nom.), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to be conducive to, produce (dat.), Pañcat., Vārtt. on Pāṇ. ii, 3, 13;
 (with adv. in सात्) to become thoroughly, Pāṇ. v, 4, 53;
to fall into a person's power, ib. 54;
 (with adv. in त्र) to fall to a person's share, ib. 55;
to produce a partic. sound (as that expressed by an onomatopoetic word in आ), Vop. vii, 88 :
Caus. -पादयति (rarely ˚ते), to cause to succeed, cause to arise, bring about, produce, effect, accomplish (with शुश्रूषाम् and gen., ‘to obey’), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to make full, complete, ŚBr.; BhP.;
to transform, make or turn into (acc.), Kathās.;
to provide or furnish with (instr.; with क्रियया, ‘to charge or entrust a person with a business’), ŚBr.; MBh. SaddhP.;
to afford to, procure for (dat. or gen.), AitBr.; MBh. &c.;
to attain, obtain, acquire, AV.; R. &c.;
to ponder on, deliberate, MBh.;
to consent, agree, Br.; ChUp. :
Desid. of Caus. -पिपादयिषति (see सम्-पिपादयिषा &c., col. 2) :
Intens. -पनीपद्यते, to fit well, Sarvad.

सम्-परि-√ ग्रह् P. Ā. -गृह्णाति, -गृह्णीते, to accept, receive, R.;
to receive in a friendly manner, MBh.;
to embrace, MW.;
to undertake, accomplish, perform, MBh.;
to take in or understand thoroughly, KaṭhUp.

सम्-परि-√ वृत् Ā. -वर्तते, to turn round, roll round (with acc.), revolve, roll (as the eyes; with हृदि or मनसि, ‘to turn over in the mind’), MBh.; Hariv.; R. &c.;
to exist, MW.;
to turn back, return, R.;
to turn back or desist from (abl.), BhP. :
Caus. -वर्तयति, to lead round, R.;
to wring (the hands), Divyāv.

(-परि- √ 5. इ) P. -पर्येति, to go round, circumambulate, R.;
to embrace, contain, AV.;
to deliberate, ponder, KaṭhUp.

सम्-√ पश् P. Ā. -पश्यति, ˚ते (occurring only in present; cf. सं-√ दृश्),
to see at the same time, survey (Ā. ‘to look at each other’, also = ‘to be together’), RV.; TS.; AV.;
to see, behold, perceive, recognize (यस्य सम्-पश्यतः, ‘before whose eyes’), Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to look at, inspect, review, ib.;
to see i.e. admit into one's presence, receive, MBh.; R.;
to look upon as, regard as, (two acc.), MBh.;
to attend to, ponder, consider, Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to count over or up, calculate, recapitulate, TS.; ŚBr.

सम्-√ पीड् P. -पीडयति, to compress, press or squeeze together, torment, harass, force (ind.p. -पीड्य = ‘by pressure or force’, ‘forcibly’), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to reckon up, calculate together, Sūryas.; Kull.;
 (in astron.) to obscure, eclipse (cf. below).

सम्-√ पूज् Caus. -पूजयति, to salute deferentially, honour greatly, revere, Mn.; MBh. &c. ;
to present respectfully with (instr.), Hit.;
to praise, commend, MBh.

सम्-√ पॄ Pass. -पूर्यते, to be completely filled, become quite full, ŚBr. :
Caus. पूरयति to fill completely, make full, Pañcat.; Kathās.;
to complete (a number), Lāṭy.;
to fill (with noise), MBh.;
to fulfil (a desire), Kathās.

सम्-√ पृच् P. Ā. -पृणक्ति, -पृङ्क्ते (Ved. also Impv. -पिपृग्धि; Pot. -पिपृच्यात्; inf. -पृ॑चः),
to mix together, commingle, bring into contact, connect, unite (Ā. and Pass., ‘to be mixed &c.’; ‘to be in contact or connected or united’), RV. &c. &c.;
to fill up, fill or satiate or endow or present with (instr.; Ā. and Pass., ‘to be filled or presented with’), RV.; AV.; TBr.

सम्-प्र-√ काश् Ā. -काशते, to become manifest, be visible, appear;
to shine, glitter, MBh.; R. :
Caus. -काशयति, to illuminate, make manifest, discover, Lalit.

सम्-प्र-√ कृ P. Ā. -करोति, -कुरुते, to produce or effect together, Car.;
to perform, begin, MBh.;
to effect, render, cause anything to become (with two acc.), R.

सम्-प्र-√ ग्रह् P. Ā. -गृह्णाति, -गृह्णीते, to hold forth or stretch forth together, ŚBr.;
to seize or take hold of together, ib.;
to take hold of MBh.; VarBṛS.;
to accept, receive (with वचनम्, ‘to receive any one's words well or kindly’), ib.; Yājñ.

सम्-प्र-√ चर् P. -चरति, to advance, begin to move, R.;
to go on, be carried on, take place, MBh.; BhP. :
Caus. -चारयति, to dismiss, Hcat.

सम्-प्र-√ जन् Ā. -जायते, to be produced, spring up, arise from (abl.), R.; Pañcat.;
to exist, be existent, Pañcat.;
to be born again, MBh.

P. Ā. -णयति, ˚ते to bring together, collect, raise (taxes), MBh.;
to compose, ib.;
 (with दण्डम्) to apply the rod, inflict punishment on (loc.), Mn. vii, 16.

(-प्रति- √ 5. इ) P. -प्रत्येति, to go towards, arrive at, come to a firm conviction, believe firmly in, trust in (gen.), R.; Bhaṭṭ.;
 Pass. -प्रतीयते, to be meant or understood, Pat. :
Caus. -प्रत्याययति, to cause to be meant or understood by, ib.

सम्-प्रति-√ पद् Ā. -पद्यते, to go towards together, go near to, approach, arrive at (acc.), Gaut.; Suśr.;
to addict one's self to, indulge in (acc.), Pañcat.;
to attain to, obtain, recover, R.; Hariv.;
to be fully agreed about, agree upon, assent to (acc. or loc.), MBh.; R.;
to consider, regard as (two acc.), Kum.;
to come to pass, arise, MW.;
to bring about, perform, accomplish, MBh. :
Caus. -पादयति, to cause to come to or receive, bestow, grant, give over to (gen. or loc.), MBh.; BhP.

P. -तिष्ठति to stand firmly on, rely on (loc.), MBh. :
Caus. -ष्ठापयति, to enclose, confine (as cows), MBh.;
to concentrate in (loc.), ChUp.;
to make firm, establish, MBh.;
to found, introduce, BhP.

सम्-प्र-√ 1. दा P. Ā. -ददाति, -दत्ते, (ind.p. -दायम्), to give completely up or deliver wholly over, surrender, give (also in marriage), PañcavBr.; MBh. &c.;
to transmit, hand down by tradition, impart, teach, MBh.; KātyŚr., Sch.; Cat.;
to grant, bestow, MBh. :
Caus. -दापयति, to cause to give over or transmit, R. :
Desid. -दित्सति, to wish to give over, Nir.

सम्-प्र-√ धृ Caus. -धारयति, to direct towards, deliver over to (dat.), MBh.;
 (with बुद्धिम्) to fix the mind or thoughts steadily upon (loc.), determine, resolve, settle, decide, ib.; Śiś.;
 (with or without बुद्ध्या, मनसा, or हृदये) to ponder, reflect, consider, deliberate or think about (acc.), Mn.; MBh.; Kāv. &c.:
Pass. -धार्यते, to be fixed upon or determined, MBh.

सम्-प्र-√ पद् Ā. -पद्यते (in some forms also P.), to go towards or enter together, approach, enter (acc.), AitBr.; BhP.;
to set out (on a journey acc.), Hariv.;
to betake one's self or have recourse to (acc.), MBh.; Hariv.; BhP.;
to succeed, be accomplished, Pañcat.;
to become, be turned into (-सात्), Bhaṭṭ.;
to set about, begin, MW.

सम्-प्र-√ मुह् P. Ā. -मुह्यति, ˚ते to become completely stupefied or embarrassed, be perplexed or unconscious, MBh.;
to be obscured or darkened, R. :
Caus. -मोहयति, to completely perplex, confuse, embarrass, MBh.

सम्-प्र-√ यम् P. Ā. -यच्छति, ˚ते, to offer or present or bestow together (Ā. also, ‘mutually’), give or present to (dat. gen. accord. to Pāṇ. i, 3, 55 also instr.), RV. &c. &c.;
to give in marriage, MBh.;
to give back, restore, R.

सम्-प्र-√ या P. याति, to proceed or set off together, to advance towards, go to (acc. with or without प्रति), ŚāṅkhŚr.; MBh. &c.;
to move, revolve (as the heavenly bodies), Sūryas.;
to go (together) to any state or condition (acc.), VarBṛS.

सम्-प्र-√ युज् P. Ā. -युनक्ति, -य्न्ङ्क्ते, to yoke or join together, yoke, harness, MBh.; R.;
to employ, make use of BhP.;
to perform, execute (a song), L.;
to instigate, incite, induce to (instr.), R. :
Pass. -युज्यते, to be joined or connected with (instr.), be added or attached, Nir.; Hariv. &c.;
to be united sexually, Rājat.;
to be implicated in (instr.), Yājñ. :
Caus. -योजयति, to join together, connect with (instr.), MBh.; Sāh. ;
to equip, prepare, Hariv.

सम्-प्र-√ वद् P. Ā. -वदति, ˚ते (Ved. inf. -वदितोस्), to pronounce aloud, PañcavBr.;
 (P.) to utter cries together, sing together, Pāṇ. i, 3, 48, Sch.;
 (Ā.) to talk or converse together, Bhaṭṭ.;
 Caus. वादयति See below.

सम्-प्र-√ विश् P. -विशति (ep. also ˚ते), to enter into together or completely (with मानसम्, or ध्यानम्, ‘to be lost in thought’), ĀśvGṛ.; MBh. &c.;
to have commerce or intercourse with (acc.), MBh.;
to be sexually united with (acc.), Mn.; MBh. :
Caus. -वेशयति, to cause to enter, introduce, lead into (acc. or loc.), R.; Hariv. &c.

सम्-प्र-√ वृत् Ā. -वर्तते, to come forth, arise, be produced from (abl.), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
 (with मनसि) to turn or think over in the mind, think deeply about, R.;
to begin, commence (said of persons and things), set about, prepare for (dat. loc., or inf.), MBh.; R. &c.;
to take place, happen, R.;
to act, proceed, deal with (loc.), R.; MārkP.; Sāh.;
to go against, assail, attack, MW.;
to be present or near at hand, ib. :
Caus. वर्तयति, to cause to proceed or go forward, spread about, circulate, set in motion or action, MBh.; BhP.; Rājat.;
to undertake, begin, MBh.; Hariv.

सम्-प्र-√ सह् P. -सहति (fut. -सहिष्यति, or -सक्ष्यति v.l. -शक्ष्यति), to have power over, become a match for, withstand, check, curb, restrain, MBh.;
to endure, tolerate, ib.;
to overcome, ib.

सम्-प्र-√ स्था Ā. -तिष्ठते, to take up a position together (before the altar), ŚāṅkhBr.;
to set out together, depart, proceed, advance, approach, go to (acc. or loc.), PraśnUp.; MBh. &c.:
Caus. स्थापयति, to dispatch, send out to (acc.), R.

सम्-प्र-√ हृ P. Ā. -हरति, ˚ते, to hurl or throw together, hurl upon (dat. or loc.), MBh.;
to attack, assail, strike at, rush upon (acc. or loc.);
 Ā. (m.c. also P.) to strike at mutually, come to blows, fight together (cf. Pāṇ. i, 3, 15,

(-प्र-√ आप्) P. -प्राप्नोति, to reach or attain fully to, arrive at, effect, accomplish, ŚBr. &c. &c.;
to get, obtain, acquire, partake of, incur, undergo, Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to obtain as a wife or in matrimony, Kathās. :
Caus. -प्रापयति (aor. -प्रापिपन्), to cause to get or obtain, ŚBr. :
Desid. See सम्-प्रेप्सु below.

(-प्र- √ 1. इष्) P. -प्रे॑ष्यति, to send forth, throw, fling, cast, MW.;
 (in Vedic ritual) to summon, invite (cf. 2. प्रेष्), Br.; ŚrS. :
Caus. -प्रेषयति, to send forth together, send away, despatch, send, dismiss, MBh.; R. &c.;
to send a message to (gen.), MBh.;
to direct (the thoughts) towards (loc.), Lalit.

सम्-√ प्लु Ā. -प्लवते, to flow or stream together, meet (as waters), MBh.;
to be heaped or massed together (as clouds), ChUp.;
to founder, go down (as a ship), GopBr.;
to fluctuate, waver (as the mind), Uttarar. :
Caus. -प्लावयति to cause to flow or mass together (as clouds), TS.; ŚBr.;
to melt into, mingle or merge with (instr.), AgP.;
to float over, inundate, submerge, MBh.; R.
